4. Discussion
4.1. Effects of environmental and time budget factors on SA
Our first research question was ‘environmental factors and time budget factors influence drivers’ SA and perceived safety?’ The results of this study revealed the significant effect of traffic density, road type, and time on the SA scores and perceived safety. The more complex the situation, the lower the SA and perceived safety scores. The SAGAT score measures drivers’ SA based on the correct answers regarding the driving situation, which is linked to the amount of information the drivers can retain and use to proceed with the driving task. The SART and perceived safety scores are self-reported measures of how confident and comfortable they feel in the
